    {
      "heading": "Related Work",
      "summary": "Short overview based only on the one source actually read in full: Wikipedia 'Successive over-relaxation' — SOR as variant of Gauss-Seidel with relaxation factor omega, devised by Young and Frankel (1950), Ostrowski convergence for symmetric positive-definite A for 0<omega<2, optimal omega_opt formula in terms of Jacobi radius mu and rho_GS = mu^2 relation under consistent-ordering assumptions. No claim to have read Young thesis, Varga, Golub & Van Loan, or LeVeque — those remain unchecked."
    },
    {
      "heading": "Model Problem and Discretization",
      "summary": "Minus Laplacian with f=1 on unit square, homogeneous Dirichlet, 5-point stencil on n x n interior grid, h=1/(n+1). Sizes tested: n=16, 32, 64 only."
